1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,852
Two men invented calculus at the same time.

2
00:00:02,802 --> 00:00:06,187
Then they spent the rest of their lives trying to destroy each other.

3
00:00:06,187 --> 00:00:11,354
Isaac Newton figured it out first, in 1666, but he told almost no one.

4
00:00:11,354 --> 00:00:13,468
He hid his work for decades.

5
00:00:13,468 --> 00:00:17,656
Meanwhile, Gottfried Leibniz published his version in 1684.

6
00:00:17,656 --> 00:00:19,635
His notation was cleaner.

7
00:00:19,635 --> 00:00:21,958
His system was easier to use.

8
00:00:21,958 --> 00:00:23,833
Newton was furious.

9
00:00:23,833 --> 00:00:29,437
He accused Leibniz of stealing his ideas, then stacked the Royal Society with allies to investigate.

10
00:00:29,437 --> 00:00:31,510
They ruled in Newton's favor.

11
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:33,677
Newton wrote the verdict himself.

12
00:00:33,677 --> 00:00:37,572
Leibniz died in 1716, alone, discredited.

13
00:00:37,572 --> 00:00:41,052
His funeral was attended by his secretary and no one else.

14
00:00:41,052 --> 00:00:42,843
But here is the twist.

15
00:00:42,843 --> 00:00:46,531
Every calculus textbook today uses Leibniz's notation.

16
00:00:46,531 --> 00:00:48,031
Not Newton's.

17
00:00:48,031 --> 00:00:50,645
The man who lost the war won the future.

